{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeWvCUwLCxXVyGRrAtk2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written all three candidate files, and the self-check passes. The smoke fit's ELPD-LOO is −1655.8, far behind the incumbent `personal_alternation_ideal` at −1088.2, so on the current data this model will probably lose by a wide margin. The brief asked for a simpler, higher-variance bet, and a clear loss still tells us something.\n\n**Model name:** `best_lag_copy_rule_detector`\n\n**Hypothesis:** People check each sequence for a simple copy rule: \"each flip repeats the flip k places back.\" A lag of 1 catches streaks, a lag of 2 catches HTHT alternation, and a lag of 4 catches HHTTHHTT. The better a sequence's best such rule predicts its flips, the less random it looks. People pick the sequence whose best rule fits worse. They differ only in how strongly this regularity affects their choice.\n\n**Why this one:** it goes after the critique's strongest problems in one mechanism:\n* People reject repeating patterns more than the incumbent predicts (the only discrepancy listed as surviving the FDR correction).\n* Long streaks are penalised beyond what the alternation rate explains.\n* The incumbent over-predicts how often people pick a perfectly alternating sequence.\n\n**How it's built:** each sequence gets one number: across every lag up to half its length, the highest share of flips that match the flip that many places back. Choice is a sigmoid of the difference between the two sequences. The only person-level parameter is a log-normal sensitivity, with 400 slots so the design can predict new participants.\n\n**Self-check:** it loads, has a finite log-probability, meets the data contract and finished the 100-draw single-chain smoke fit. Two warnings to note:\n* **Pareto k:** 1.3% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5, over the 1.0% tolerance, so PSIS-LOO was flagged as unreliable on the smoke fit and that ELPD may be off.\n* **Untested gates:** the check doesn't test convergence, novelty against the other models, or the 30-minute time limit; admission's full fit will.\n\nThe files are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2940,"cache_read_input_tokens":49943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2940,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":702,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8fb4eb6a-7b82-4881-bdce-4378656c6878","uuid":"ba8b4b02-a667-4f8c-868b-ce507d146a94","timestamp":"2026-10-03T02:29:53.081Z","request_id":"req_011CfeWvC48Ks9f4VL7eDhqT"}
